[00:45.13] My uncle has a country place
[00:48.86] No one knows about
[00:51.72] He says it used to be a farm
[00:55.05] Before the "Motor Law"
[00:58.05] And on Sundays I elude the eyes
[01:01.78] And hop the turbine freight
[01:04.87] To far outside the wire
[01:07.86] Where my white-haired uncle waits
[01:11.02] 
[01:31.97] Jump to the ground
[01:33.06] As the turbo slows to cross the borderline
[01:38.42] Run like the wind
[01:39.71] As excitement shivers up and down my spine
[01:45.15] Down in his barn
[01:46.44] My uncle preserved for me an old machine
[01:50.08] For 50 odd years
[01:51.75] To keep it as new has been his dearest dream
[01:59.59] I strip away the old debris
[02:02.92] That hides a shining car
[02:05.98] A brilliant red Barchetta
[02:08.53] From a better vanished time
[02:12.88] We fire up the willing engine
[02:16.26] Responding with a roar
[02:19.63] Tires spitting gravel
[02:21.97] I commit my weekly crime
[02:25.70] 
[02:40.98] Wind in my hair
[02:45.45] Shifting and drifting
[02:50.86] Mechanical music
[02:56.86] Adrenaline surge
[02:59.28] 
[03:06.25] Well-weathered leather
[03:07.76] Hot metal and oil
[03:09.32] The scented country air
[03:12.69] Sunlight on chrome
[03:14.23] The blur of the landscape
[03:16.15] Every nerve aware
[03:18.43] 
[03:54.14] Suddenly ahead of me
[03:57.28] Across the mountainside
[04:00.43] A gleaming alloy air car
[04:03.22] Shoots towards me, two lanes wide
[04:07.14] I spin around with shrieking tires
[04:10.60] To run the deadly race
[04:13.78] Go screaming through the valley
[04:16.57] As another joins the chase
[04:20.33] 
[04:40.62] Drive like the wind
[04:42.33] Straining the limits of machine and man
[04:47.12] Laughing out loud with fear and hope
[04:50.02] I've got a desperate plan
[04:53.49] At the one-lane bridge
[04:54.91] I leave the giants stranded at the riverside
[05:00.03] Race back to the farm
[05:02.08] To dream with my uncle at the fireside
[05:06.85] 